<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2013/05/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>DllExport.Lite</id>
    <version>$-version-$</version>
    <title>.NET DllExport (lite)</title>
    <authors>github.com/3F/DllExport</authors>
    <license type="file">LICENSE.txt</license>
    <owners>reg</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/3F/DllExport</projectUrl>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/3F/DllExport" />
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <developmentDependency>true</developmentDependency>
    <description>.NET DllExport as a plain NuGet package: no DllExport.bat, no Manager, nothing downloaded.

        Reference the package and mark methods with [RGiesecke.DllExport.DllExport]. The build imports DllExport's usual targets with fixed defaults (RGiesecke.DllExport namespace, 3F's IL Assembler); any DllExport MSBuild property can still be set in the project.

        Installed in Visual Studio, the readable tools\init.ps1 converts projects that use UnmanagedExports or the NotepadPlusPlusPluginPack.Net template's NppPlugin.DllExport, and adds the ARM64 platform. Without Visual Studio, run tools\Convert-ToDllExportLite.ps1 by hand.

        For full configuration through the Manager, use the main DllExport package and DllExport.bat instead:
        https://github.com/3F/DllExport</description>
    <summary>.NET DllExport as a plain NuGet package: no DllExport.bat, no Manager</summary>
    <tags>DllExport unmanaged-exports ildasm ilasm coreclr exported-functions native arm64 unmanaged-export</tags>
    <releaseNotes> changelog: https://github.com/3F/DllExport/blob/master/changelog.txt </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) 2009-2015  Robert Giesecke | Copyright (c) 2016-2026  Denis Kuzmin &lt;x-3F@outlook.com&gt; github/3F </copyright>
  </metadata>
</package>
